1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,815
Trading ideas start in conversations.

2
00:00:03,015 --> 00:00:04,255
Someone posts a call.

3
00:00:04,255 --> 00:00:05,438
Someone argues back.

4
00:00:05,438 --> 00:00:08,199
But testing that idea means a wallet, a deposit,

5
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:09,138
and real risk.

6
00:00:09,388 --> 00:00:10,788
Strike Agent changes that.

7
00:00:10,788 --> 00:00:12,758
Test the idea right where it happens:

8
00:00:12,758 --> 00:00:13,167
on X.

9
00:00:13,617 --> 00:00:16,348
Mention Strike Agent with a market, a virtual margin,

10
00:00:16,348 --> 00:00:17,056
and leverage.

11
00:00:17,056 --> 00:00:19,481
Paper long Bitcoin, a hundred dollars, two-x.

12
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:22,079
This is a real receipt from our first live test.

13
00:00:22,079 --> 00:00:23,038
Paper position one.

14
00:00:23,038 --> 00:00:23,709
Long Bitcoin.

15
00:00:23,709 --> 00:00:25,531
A hundred dollars of margin at two-x,

16
00:00:25,531 --> 00:00:27,400
entered at the live Strike mark price.

17
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,413
And no real order.

18
00:00:28,663 --> 00:00:29,265
In that test,

19
00:00:29,265 --> 00:00:32,532
our server received the mention six and a half seconds after it was posted,

20
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:35,047
and opened the position thirty nine milliseconds later.

21
00:00:35,597 --> 00:00:39,231
Every X account gets its own ten thousand dollar virtual account.

22
00:00:39,231 --> 00:00:42,424
Go long or short on Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana or Cardano,

23
00:00:42,424 --> 00:00:43,455
at up to five-x.

24
00:00:43,655 --> 00:00:46,043
Check your portfolio, pull a fresh price, close a position,

25
00:00:46,043 --> 00:00:48,581
and review your history and stats, all with simple commands.

26
00:00:48,781 --> 00:00:50,215
Commands are strict and exact,

27
00:00:50,215 --> 00:00:51,926
so a reply only does what you typed.

28
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:54,019
And only you can close your own positions.

29
00:00:54,569 --> 00:00:56,618
Under the hood, X sends a signed webhook.

30
00:00:56,618 --> 00:00:59,256
We verify it, drop duplicates, and queue it safely.

31
00:00:59,406 --> 00:01:00,922
Then we read a fresh Strike mark,

32
00:01:00,922 --> 00:01:03,643
apply simulated fees and slippage, update your paper ledger,

33
00:01:03,643 --> 00:01:04,863
and reply in the thread.

34
00:01:05,013 --> 00:01:06,315
Stale prices are rejected,

35
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:09,214
and a duplicate delivery never creates a duplicate trade.

36
00:01:09,764 --> 00:01:11,400
And when you're ready for the real thing,

37
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,659
every receipt links straight to Strike's own trading app.

38
00:01:13,659 --> 00:01:15,056
You decide, and you trade there.

39
00:01:15,707 --> 00:01:16,580
Strike Agent.

40
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:17,515
Practice on X.

41
00:01:17,515 --> 00:01:18,663
Trade on Strike.
